{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/407027-markings-for-the-forbidden-arcanoi","id":407027,"title":"Markings for the Forbidden Arcanoi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T15:05:54-08:00","id":407027,"title":"Markings for the Forbidden Arcanoi","content":"It seems the original Player's Guide left out markings for Flux, Intimation and Mnemosynis. Any word on what those are? There are also no markings for Dark or Jade Arcanoi as far as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T17:20:27-08:00","id":407150,"title":"","content":"Flux sprang from Kinesis, so it probably has something akin to the red welt marks, Intimation users have a bright green left eye, and Mnemoi don't blink.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: I can't seem to find anything on Dark and Jade Acranoi (or Risen). Hopefully this oversight will be addressed in Wr20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 02-16-2015, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T23:54:54-08:00","id":412490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/407027-markings-for-the-forbidden-arcanoi?p=407150#post407150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flux sprang from Kinesis, so it probably has something akin to the red welt marks, Intimation users have a bright green left eye, and Mnemoi don't blink. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, the Alchemists have no distinguishing mark (at least according to the LARP rules). But most of them are obsessive tinkerers, and will happily go on and on about their latest project. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:07:06-08:00","id":418803,"title":"","content":"My Storyteller has used these:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0305jadedark.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0305jadedark.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Jade and Dark Arcanos Markings </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0305jadedark.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0305jadedark.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They're not official, but they're cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:04:34-08:00","id":419788,"title":"","content":"I found those when I was Googling around. I like them too. I'm letting a player in my new Wraith game use Flux, and I wanted an actual Arcanos marking for him. &quot;Nothing&quot; seems really lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:08:45-08:00","id":420405,"title":"","content":"What Arcanos has the &quot;one eye is poisonous green&quot; mark? I thought it was in one of the source books for Flux. I can't remember where exactly. It was in the context of having high levels of two Arcanoi with similar markings. Essentially answering &quot;If both of my eyes are jet black and one of them is green are they both black or is one green and one black?&quot; Answer: One is green, one is black.<br /> <br /> Anyone who has Keening essentially has no Arcanos marking.... Carrying a lute REALLY doesn't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:12:28-08:00","id":420408,"title":"","content":"Like someone mentioned above Intimation, practiced by the Solicitors Guild, has the marking of the left eye turning green.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:15:16-08:00","id":420641,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of the three Arcanoi with &quot;external&quot; markings, like bits of costuming. Keening's musical instrument, Pandemonium's black cloak and Usury's scales are all kinda.. odd. I'd much rather have physical markings like almost all the others do. Phantasm and Puppetry, with their behavioral markings are also not my favorites. I'm not even super sure how to run Moliate's &quot;soft corpus&quot; or &quot;inhuman perfection&quot; compared to the rather straight-forward markings of Argos, Lifeweb, Castigate, Embody, Fatalism, Outrage, Inhabit, Intimation and Mnemosynis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:27:21-08:00","id":420675,"title":"","content":"Guildbook Haunters says the real marks of Pandemonium are strange things happening to one's Corpus, like tumors or insects plaguing the Wraith. Also possible are time and spatial distortions around the ghost. In other words, they say that uncontrollable Pandemonium effects manifested on the Corpus are the true markings of Pandemonium. The billowing cloaks are meant to hide these. My favorite example, of a rarer type of manifestation, is of a Haunter that leaves afterimages of himself trailing behind him, each one younger than the previous, the last one a small child.<br /> <br /> I suppose if other Guildbooks were published, we would see new, &quot;real&quot; markings for some of these Arcanoi. Hopefully Wraith 20 will address this, as they already did with Usury. Instead of only speaking in precise numerical terms (which they do), Usurers have a mark etched on their lips and hands of the energy they transferred, in an appropriate color to mark borrowing or giving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:34:11-08:00","id":420682,"title":"","content":"Oh, I really like that new Usury marking. Very cool. I'm still not a fan of the Pandemonium marking. It's too unspecific. &quot;Random manifestations of creepyness&quot; isn't something you can be on the watch for, like black-stained fingers or unblinking eyes or a green glowing left eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:49:26-08:00","id":420833,"title":"","content":"We used a weird voice effect for Keening. Like feedback or back echo when the character talked.<br /> <br /> Having bugs erupt out of your skin and crawl up your nose while trying to have a polite conversation seems like it would be pretty noticeable. Or starting to talk backwards. Similar things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:10:51-08:00","id":421280,"title":"","content":"We're doing a bit of rework on the Arcanos markings to make them feel a little more logical.<br /> <br /> Anyone want to guess why the green eye was the mark of the Solicitors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:46:51-08:00","id":421339,"title":"","content":"Pandemoniums markings are that it twists the mind and perceptions of the user most common are Spatial Distortion, which messes with you senses and makes it harder to judge distances etc, Chronical Fatigue, which messes up your perception of time, and Hallucinations, which should be obvious. For some Haunters these symptoms become so bad that they start to twist their corpus in ways suitable for each infliction. A Haunter with Spatial Distortion could look like his mask and other worn things are just beneath the surface of his somewhat translucent Corpus, while one with Chronical Fatigue can at extreme cases have those afterimages following him and one with Hallucinations could have almost anything including being insect ridden or have his Corpus filled with roiling storm clouds that occasionally rumble with lightning.<br /> <br /> All in all Pandemoniums, or if your a Haunter Wyldings, markings are well covered and excellent in both concept and execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:04:14-08:00","id":421842,"title":"","content":"The big problem with Markings is that they should get those with high dots in forbidden Arcanoi forged for violating the Dictum Mortuum....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T10:24:00-08:00","id":421931,"title":"","content":"And that is why practitioners of such should really avoid loyal legionnaires and hierarchs in general. That is to say that is why those practicing forbidden Arcanoi, Flux, Mnemosysis and Intimation, tend to go deep underground and hide amongst the renegades and heretics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:38:09-08:00","id":422123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/407027-markings-for-the-forbidden-arcanoi?p=421280#post421280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone want to guess why the green eye was the mark of the Solicitors?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed it had something to with greed/envy. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T03:49:12-08:00","id":422794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/407027-markings-for-the-forbidden-arcanoi?p=422123#post422123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always assumed it had something to with greed/envy.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought as well... Intimation is all about manipulation of desire. As for the single eye, I am not sure. I am reminded of Gatsby's light, to be sure...<br /> <br /> People with heterochromia are sometimes linked to witchcraft (the Solicitor's guild is very cultish) faeries, and having spiritual powers (some native american tribes supposed that someone with one blue eye and one brown eye could see both heaven and earth at the same time)<br /> <br /> The sideways glance is often associated with desire as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}